      "item": "theoreticalsciences:cracking_tower",
      "title": "Cracking Tower",
      "text": "Long carbon chains heated for half a second and quenched: they break into short ones, ethylene above all.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 2$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Set the furnace temperature and the steam ratio. Each product has its temperature (ethylene about 1100 K, propylene 1000 K): its share must reach 60%. Above about 1150 K coke builds up and fouls the Zeolite Catalyst (it wears ten times as fast) - steam keeps it down."
    },
